{
  "id": "COMPOUND:471 - PROTEIN:802",
  "verbalization": "Gallamine triethiodide appears to enhance the efficacy of multiple drugs by promoting their interaction with Chromium, which in turn targets the Proteasome subunit beta type-5. This relationship is supported by a consistent pathway where Gallamine triethiodide increases the effectiveness of enfortumab vedotin, epicillin, and basifungin, all of which share a common downstream effect on Chromium. Chromium is known to act as a substrate for the Proteasome subunit beta type-5, suggesting a potential mechanism involving the regulation of protein degradation. The evidence points to a hierarchical interaction where Gallamine triethiodide may modulate the activity of these drugs through a shared pathway that ultimately influences the target protein. The integration of these findings highlights a possible role for Gallamine triethiodide in enhancing the therapeutic effect of these compounds by targeting a common downstream effector, Chromium, which is essential for the function of the Proteasome subunit beta type-5.",
